[resource]
script = ExtResource("3_elk2l")
discs = Array[ExtResource("1_67ixv")]([SubResource("Resource_pn6q1")])
title = "Advanced Invasion OST"
liner_notes = "I view this game as pretty much an album with a game attached, albeit an album of video game music. Most of the music was written first and that guided the development of the game.

The primary inspiration is the collage-like nature of the music accompanying games uploaded to the YoYoGames Sandbox. As GameMaker had MIDI support, developers at the time would lift MIDI covers of video game music and put them directly into their game, resulting in a blend of extremely iconic - but highly disparate - tracks.

Now of course everyone knows better. That, and we are abated by the ever-looming spectre of the Digital Millennium Copyright Act. Luckily, I know how to make my own music now, but I still wanted to capture the feel of those early days.

My approach, therefore, was to use MIDI exclusively. Each track is a GS-compliant MIDI file written for and then rendered (via SC VA in this case) by an SC-88 Pro (followed by just a little bit of audio manipulation to get it looping). Working to a single sound set is limiting, sure, but it comes with its own charm. Indeed, it's one of my favourite mediums. But more importantly for that collage-like quality, it makes it easier to combine diverse instrumentation like orchestras and synths without sounding too incoherent.

I chose the SC-88 Pro due to its shared lineage with the Microsoft GM Wavetable Synth that all our stolen MIDIs played on back on back in the day. The SC-55 is closer, to that sound, of course, but I felt an upgrade to the next generation was fitting. It's a little more \"advanced\" if you will (hehe).

Regardless, I hope this soundtrack sounds like I just stole a bunch of MIDIs and put them into a game, because that's the sound I was going for (just without the actual stealing part). The use of a few shared motifs/melodies across the tracks hopefully then takes it just over the line into being a complete and self-contained work of art. Consistent, but inconsistent in equal measures.

You be the judge.

(By the way, I released all this music under Creative Commons. Please, use those terms to steal it and put it in your own games! Click \"Download Album\" for more details)"
download_url = "https://speedyvelcro.com/music/advanced-invasion-ost/"
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://c4mywst67rhre"
